Subject: Re: Recap + next steps: multi-tool calling & fallback patterns for FinEdge

Adding a few practical patterns we'll bring to the session — pasteable notes for your architects: 

A) Tool definition (canonical)- name: account_lookup
- inputs: { user_id, account_scope }
- outputs: { account_summary, last_4, status }
- idempotent: true

B) Parallel fan-out (non-mutating) pattern1) Receive user prompt -> generate tool-intent detection (1-2ms pre-check)2) Fan-out: call knowledge_search + enrichment_service in parallel (set deadline 300ms)3) Await both with select-first-success then run top-K reranker on the best passages4) If reranker not back within SLO, return the preliminary (embedding-based) best answer and stream update when reranker results arrive

C) Mutating operations (payments)- Strict sequence: validate -> pre-authorize -> initiate_payment (single writer)- Use a transaction id (client-generated) and idempotency keys at each step- Circuit-breaker: if payment gateway errors > 5/min, switch to manual queue and notify ops

D) Error handling & UX patterns- Transient errors: exponential backoff with capped retries (3) + user-visible toast: "We're retrying — some results may be delayed."- Permanent failures: fallback to cached data or human route (create ticket) and surface a clear explanation to the user- Observability: emit token-level latency + tool success metrics to Redwood Console and add a rerank-failure alert (threshold > 5% for 24h)

E) Embedding + reranker pipeline- Indexing cadence: nightly bulk + incremental nearline for new docs- Retrieval: ANN (k=100) -> embed-similarity prune -> cross-encoder top-5 rerank -> final answer composition

Small code sketch (pseudo):

// server SDK flow
const tools = [accountLookup, knowledgeSearch, enrichment];
const results = await Promise.allSettled(tools.map(t => t.call(input)));
const best = selectTop(results.filter(r => r.status === 'fulfilled'));;
if (!best.rerankerComplete) { sendPrelimResponse(best.embedResult); }
when(rerankerComplete, sendUpdate(best.final));

